From 0fc8f4917044e859315a32e2033e9828f8f722bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WaleWangPW <396218656@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:56:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] feat(task): port terminal DB-only archived-resource
 actions

Adds the three terminal actions that consume the retained-anchor identity
built in Task05: exact-generation stale pending move cancellation,
absent-target release admission sealed behind central physicaldelete,
and environment retirement as one serializable exact-set transaction.

- Models: archived_resource_release.go and archived_resource_environment_retirement.go
  with strict canonical JSON, immutable digest binding, fourteen-column per-row
  generation, and the released lifecycle state.
- Physicaldelete inventory: ActionReleaseAbsent routed through ExecutorNone with
  the sealed absence proof; types.go carries the new action, executor, and denial.
- Repository: CancelStaleArchivedResourcePendingMove CAS-clears the target row only;
  ReleaseAbsentArchivedResourceAnchor verifies inventory absence and CAS-transitions
  retained -> released in one serializable transaction; RetireStaleArchivedResourceEnvironmentReference
  scans workspace-group inventory for the four accepted states and rejects any v2/v3
  participant including non-coordinators before deleting exact repository rows.
- Service: three metadata-only methods gated by archivedResourceReconcileOn /
  archivedResourcePhysicalReleaseOn; terminal session precheck for the cancel.
- Handlers: three new routes registered under admin auth, gated by the same two flags.
- Tests: model canonical/drift tests, repository fail-closed tests (inventory
  retention, header drift, sibling isolation, unknown workspace group state),
  service disabled-by-default tests, handler flag-and-shape tests.
